# Ironless linear axis (examples/linear_axis.conf: 60 mm electrical period,
# 5 um encoder, 1 m stroke with end stops) with one reference mark at
# -477 mm. Starts autophased (enc_fb0.state 1), jogs at -120 mm/s across
# the mark, which switches commutation to absolute (state 3) using
# conf0.mot_fb_offset, and back to the start: no fault, no following-error
# step at the switch (fault0.pos_error is pid0.pos_error, sampled across
# the mark), never at an end stop. The larger peaks of pid0.pos_error are
# the instantaneous velocity steps at the start and the reversal.
@args --drive examples/linear_axis.conf --sim examples/linear_axis_sim.txt
debug_level 0
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
# probe phasing (fb_switch0.phase_mode 1) takes about 2 s on this carriage
run 2.5
enc_fb0.state
lcnc 1 -120
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.05 3.7
@sample fault0.pos_error 0.005 0.4
hv0.sim_abs_pos
enc_fb0.state
fb_switch0.current_com_pos
lcnc 1 120
@sample pid0.pos_error 0.05 4.1
lcnc 1 0
run 0.5
hv0.sim_abs_pos
pid0.pos_error
hv0.sim_stop_hits
fault0.fault
@expect enc_fb0.state[1] == 1
@expect enc_fb0.state[2] == 3
@expect fb_switch0.current_com_pos == 1
@expect hv0.sim_abs_pos[1] ~ -51.5 0.3
@expect hv0.sim_abs_pos ~ 0 0.3
@expect max|fault0.pos_error| < 0.002
@expect max|pid0.pos_error| < 0.025
@expect hv0.sim_stop_hits == 0
@expect fault0.fault == 0
